Xocean
As an ocean data company using uncrewed surface vessels (USVs), Xocean's culture is deeply tied to sustainability and remote technology. 
      Work Culture:
        ◦ Purpose-Driven: The culture is centered on making a positive environmental impact through renewable energy data collection.
        ◦ Remote-First: The company operates a primarily remote working model, which supports a better work-life balance for traditional seafarers.
        ◦ Inclusivity: Xocean reports having a gender-employment ratio significantly higher than the maritime industry average.
    • Team Structure:
        ◦ Specialized Hubs: Teams are distributed across international offices (Ireland, UK, US, Canada, Norway, Australia).
        ◦ Functional Focus: The structure is divided into technology development, operations, and data analytics.
        ◦ Current State: Recent reviews mention a disconnect between senior leadership and staff following a 20% workforce reduction in late 2025. 
          
Wayflyer
Wayflyer is a high-growth fintech company where the culture is often described as high-pressure but rewarding. 
    • Work Culture:
        ◦ High Ambition: Core values include being "ambitious overachievers" and "excellent operators".
        ◦ Demanding Environment: The culture is fast-paced and can be high-pressure, particularly in sales roles with aggressive targets.
        ◦ Transparency Focus: Promotes a "Kind over Nice" value, encouraging candid but respectful feedback.
        ◦ Instability Issues: Employee feedback frequently cites high turnover in senior leadership and recent redundancies as sources of cultural strain.
    •      Team Structure:
        ◦ Cross-Functional: Teams are designed to be cross-functional to move with "speed and quality".
        ◦ Sales Model: In sales, they often use a 1:1 pairing of Account Executives (AEs) and Business Development Representatives (BDRs).
        ◦ Hybrid Approach: Most teams operate on a hybrid model (3–4 days in-office) to maintain access to senior leadership. 
